{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Its provision</b> — the land will be pleasant and blessed. And the reason for mentioning צידה is from the root of צדה לדרך (provision for the road), and this word comes in the sense of 'from every direction,' for a blessing will be found in every צדה that passersby take from it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 132, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:37.770183181Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}